## Key Learnings
1. Pekko ByteString take, drop and slice never fail on out-of-range arguments; they clamp, so a "range failure" outcome has no Pekko oracle (ByteStringSpec.scala:361-631).
2. IO.scala is only a three-member accessor, and each protocol extension creates its own manager (Tcp.scala:654, Udp.scala:236, UdpConnected.scala:174, Dns.scala:242).
3. SimpleDnsManager.postStop only cancels the cleanup timer, so a pending-request result on DNS manager shutdown is not Pekko behavior.
4. The TCP after-connect socket option spec is disabled with ignore in TcpConnectionSpec.scala:109, so no active Pekko oracle covers it.
5. TcpConnectionSpec shows two writes pending at one selector wake-up arriving as one Received (TcpConnectionSpec.scala:122-134); no documented boundary guarantee was found.
